    fix: a lock the adjudicator cannot open is an ERROR, never RESIDUE. Addresses CF-259.
    
    scripts/board_lock.py mapped EVERY non-held flock_probe result to RESIDUE, so a
    lock file this process cannot even open was reported as a clean negative — "no
    barrier, proceed with the board write". Measured at HEAD 62969c8 with a mktemp
    dir holding a 0-byte .lock, chmod 000:
    
      before  RESIDUE consumers=0 commits_after_mtime=unknown      rc=0
      after   ERROR lock=<tmp>/board/.lock probe=open-failed is not a clean negative — the lock state is UNKNOWN
                                                                   rc=3
    
    - scripts/board_lock.py: adjudicate() returns a Verdict(line, exit_code) and
      main() propagates it. The three genuine outcomes keep their byte-identical
      tokens and exit 0 (ABSENT, HELD holder=..., RESIDUE consumers=<n>
      commits_after_mtime=<n|unknown>); a probe that could not run — open-failed or
      a non-contention errno — prints the single ERROR line and exits 3. A partial
      /proc fd scan stays a clean observation by design: only the flock probe's own
      `error` result becomes ERROR, so degraded observation is not turned into a
      non-zero exit wholesale.
    - The module header's premise is corrected: .coding-hermes/board/.lock is
      ignored by .gitignore (line 20); it never had "no ignore rule".
    - tests/selftest.sh section 33 gains one arm: a 0-byte lock chmod 000 must not
      print ^RESIDUE, must carry the ERROR token, and must exit non-zero. On a user
      that can read mode-000 files (root) the arm prints a named SKIP with its uid
      instead of passing silently. The existing RESIDUE and HELD arms are unchanged.
    - docs/BOARD.md and docs/handbook/chapters/M4-board.md (III.M4.S1) now document
      four outcomes and the exit-code table, and the chapter's degraded-observation
      paragraph states this measurement is an ERROR verdict with a non-zero exit
      rather than being folded into RESIDUE. Line references re-verified against
      the committed file (adjudicate :166-185, ERROR :175-180, RESIDUE :181-185).
    
    Evidence: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (exit 0), 405 PASS rows,
    including "PASS  unreadable lock -> not RESIDUE, exit 3 (ERROR lock=...
    probe=open-failed is not a clean negative — the lock state is UNKNOWN)";
    bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (7 warning(s)).
